    "打開「允許完整取用」" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Turn on \"Allow Full Access\""
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "打开“允许完全访问”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "打開「允許完整存取」" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Turn on \"Allow Full Access\""
          }
        },
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "打开“允许完全访问”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "打開後會把錄到的聲音先放大（數位增益，約 +8 dB，放大後會限幅避免破音），同時把「這段算靜音」的判斷放寬，讓輕聲講也能被聽到。App 內聽寫與鍵盤講話都有效；iOS 沒有公開的麥克風硬體增益 API，所以是在軟體裡放大。" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "打开后会先把录到的声音放大（数字增益，约 +8 dB，放大后会限幅避免破音），同时放宽「这段算静音」的判断，让轻声说话也能被听到。App 内听写与键盘说话都有效；iOS 没有公开的麦克风硬件增益 API，所以是在软件里放大。"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "When on, recorded audio is amplified first (digital gain, about +8 dB, with a limiter so it does not clip) and the \"this counts as silence\" judgement is loosened, so speaking quietly still gets picked up. This applies both to dictation inside the app and to the keyboard. iOS has no public hardware microphone-gain API, so the amplification happens in software."
          }
        }
      }
    },
